CAKE (Common Applications Kept Enhanced) is a queue scheduler that
combines flow and host fairness, diffserv priority tins, the COBALT
AQM and link-layer overhead compensation. This plugin lets pipes of
the traffic shaper use it in place of FQ-CoDel.

The scheduler is an unofficial kernel module (cake-kmod) built for a
specific OPNsense series. If it does not match the running kernel,
the shaper keeps running with the pipes' own scheduler.

